  "outcome": {
    "ok": true,
    "turn_id": "d09_final_matched:r12:t1",
    "narration": "The floor settled into its sparse quiet. Nicco spoke the rule plainly — during shared reading, a quiet-break request needs no explanation and is answered by lowering voices.\n\nIris waited a beat. \"All right,\" she said. Nothing more, no qualification, no question. She took the rule at face value.\n\nThe two patient beds, the empty wardrobes, the bare medical cabinets — none of it had changed. The floor was still just stone and sparse furniture and the open central space, the spiral stair sitting at the perimeter. If the rule would matter later, it would be when there was something to read and someone to read it together.",
